ies market moves.","About $40.9M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 70% in the 2020 crash and 39% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 61% below its DCF fair value of $112, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 83%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $65.17 to $185 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 8.7 vs 19.3 and EV/EBITDA 8.6 vs 11.2 (sector median).","The EBIT multiple is close to its own 10-year median (-3%).","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 6.9% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $47.10 on average, 7% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% earns above the cost of capital of 7.0%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.37).","It converts 5% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 3.70x.","ROE of 6% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (9.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 5.7x net debt to EBITDA ($239.0M of cash against $4.5B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.6x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.78 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.6% over 3 years and 41.4% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 63%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 26.5% a year over five years.","Margins are contracting (-1.7% trend).","Forward indicators: a backlog worth 6% of annual revenue.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (1.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.1%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 2 purchases and 7 sales over the past year, net $14.7M sold.","It returns 18.0% a year to shareholders (18.0% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 8.8% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 16.3% of the float, 6.7 days to cover."],"people":["With about 22,300 employees, each generates about $226K of revenue, 0.6x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 12.3% a year.","That works out to $10K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $6.3M (28x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":52,"head":"Avoid: Altman Z in the distress zone (0.78).","pros":["Trades 61% below fair value of $112","Revenue grew 41.4%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 7/9","P/E 8.7x vs sector 19.3x","EV/EBITDA 8.6x vs sector 11.2x"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 5.7x","Interest coverage only 1.6x","Altman Z in the distress zone (0.78)","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","Operating margin contracting 1.7%/yr"],"flags":["Altman Z in the distress zone (0.78)"],"need":[],"buy_below":95.08,"vc":{"base":111.86,"base_src":"dcf","bear":65.17,"bull":184.82,"alt_median":11.93,"n_alt":1,"gap":9.8376,"dispersion":0.831,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (83% dispersion)","DCF is 984% above the other models' median ($11.93)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"HGV","date":"2026-11-06"}